[center][size=6][b]Mod KOTOR without the busywork.[/b][/size]
[size=4]One app. Recommended builds. Downloads and installs in the right order.[/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-mod-manager/main/docs/images/01-builds.png[/img]

[url=https://github.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-mod-manager/releases/latest]GitHub releases[/url] | [url=https://christophervr.github.io/kotor-mod-manager/]Project site[/url] | [url=https://github.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-mod-manager/issues]Support[/url][/center]

[b]KOTOR Mod Installer[/b] is a free, open-source standalone app for [b]Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic[/b] and [b]Knights of the Old Republic II: The Sith Lords[/b]. Choose a recommended community build, load its mod list, and let the app download, unpack and install the mods in order.

[b]This download is the manager, not a mod pack.[/b] It bundles no game files or community mod archives. Mods come from their original hosts using your own accounts.

[size=5][b]See it in action[/b][/size]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-mod-manager/main/docs/images/tour.gif[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]What you get[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Guided community builds:[/b] load a recommended list for KOTOR 1 or KOTOR 2 and install in its intended order.
[*][b]Automatic patching:[/b] a bundled HoloPatcher engine applies supported TSLPatcher mods without clicking through separate installers.
[*][b]A searchable library:[/b] browse installed mods, filter them and import your own archives or folders.
[*][b]Loose-file mod switches:[/b] turn supported loose-file mods off and on while keeping their files tracked.
[*][b]Conflict checks:[/b] see overlapping files and declared incompatibilities before they become surprises.
[*][b]Built-in updates:[/b] check GitHub for new app releases and update from inside the app.
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-mod-manager/main/docs/images/library-search.gif[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]Get started[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Choose the [b]Windows[/b] or [b]Linux x86_64[/b] Main file, use [b]Manual download[/b], and extract the ZIP into its own folder. [b]Do not install this app through Vortex or extract it into your game folder.[/b]
[*][b]Windows:[/b] run [b]KOTOR-Mod-Installer.exe[/b]. [b]Linux:[/b] run [b]KOTOR-Mod-Installer-linux-x86_64[/b]. If needed, allow it to run in Properties > Permissions, or run [b]chmod +x KOTOR-Mod-Installer-linux-x86_64[/b] first. No separate Python or Node installation is needed.
[*]Open [b]Settings > Game Installs[/b] and choose your KOTOR 1 and/or KOTOR 2 installation folders.
[*]Sign in to [b]DeadlyStream[/b] under Account. For builds containing Nexus mods, add your personal Nexus API key under [b]Settings > Nexus[/b].
[*]In [b]Mod Builds[/b], choose a build, click [b]Load Mod List[/b], then [b]Download & Install[/b]. Follow any download or installation choices the app shows.
[/list]

[b]Back up your saves before modding.[/b] For a new build, start with a clean game installation and follow that build's requirements. The app does not make every combination of mods compatible.

[size=5][b]Accounts and downloads[/b][/size]
A DeadlyStream account is needed for mods hosted there. Nexus-hosted mods use [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/users/myaccount?tab=api]your personal Nexus API key[/url]. Keep it private.

[list]
[*][b]Nexus Premium:[/b] automatic Nexus downloads.
[*][b]Free Nexus account:[/b] the app opens each mod page for you. Click [b]Mod manager download[/b] on that mod's page to continue. This is for downloading mods inside the app, not for installing this manager through Vortex.
[*][b]Download limits:[/b] if Nexus limits interrupt a build, wait and retry. Completed downloads are kept.
[*][b]Other hosts:[/b] many links download automatically. Some sites need a browser login or a manual download; the app shows when your help is needed.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Know what can be undone[/b][/size]
Loose-file mods can be disabled and restored from the library. TSLPatcher and HoloPatcher mods change shared files in place. These are recorded as [b]baked[/b] and are [b]not cleanly reversible by switching them off[/b]. Keep backups and plan your build before installing patcher-based mods.

[size=5][b]Requirements and safety[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Your own copy of KOTOR 1 and/or KOTOR 2 and enough disk space for the build's downloads and backups.
[*][b]64-bit Windows or an x86_64 Linux desktop.[/b] Both downloads are on the Files tab and on [url=https://github.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-mod-manager/releases/latest]GitHub Releases[/url]. Linux needs GTK 3 and WebKitGTK 4.1 runtime libraries from your distribution; if launch fails, run the app from a terminal to see missing-library messages.
[*]Internet access and accounts for the hosts used by your selected build.
[*]ZIP extraction works without extra tools. For some other archives or installer formats, you may need [url=https://www.7-zip.org/]7-Zip[/url]. A custom 7-Zip path can be set in Settings.
[/list]

Release downloads are scanned with ClamAV before publication. The ZIP includes the release scan report and SHA-256 checksums. Scanning is not a guarantee of safety. Windows may warn about an unsigned application; report antivirus detections rather than disabling protection.

[size=5][b]Help, source and credits[/b][/size]
For a bug report, include the app version, your game, the selected build or mod, and what happened. The Activity screen can export logs; review them for private information before sharing. Never post API keys or passwords.

[url=https://github.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-mod-manager#readme]Full guide and FAQ[/url] | [url=https://github.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-mod-manager/issues]Report a problem[/url] | [url=https://github.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-mod-manager]Source code[/url]

The app is licensed under [b]GPL-3.0-only[/b]. It bundles the HoloPatcher engine from the PyKotor project. Community mod authors retain their own permissions and credits: downloading a mod through this app does not change its license or grant redistribution rights.

This is an unofficial fan tool, not affiliated with Nexus Mods or the game's rights holders. No game files, mod packs or DRM bypass are supplied.
